Add pinch-to-zoom and two-finger pan so the map is usable on a touchscreen.

Camera input is wired for a mouse: one pointer orbits, panning needs the right
button or a modifier key, and zoom comes only from a wheel event. Touch devices
have neither a wheel nor a right button, so on a phone or tablet the map can be
rotated and nothing else — you cannot get closer to a node or move off centre.

The canvas already uses pointer events with touch-action:none, so the gestures
map onto the existing camera model directly: a second pointer switches from
orbiting to pinch-zoom plus a pan driven by the midpoint, and lifting back to one
finger resumes orbiting from that finger's position instead of jumping. A second
finger going down also marks the gesture as moved, so a pinch is never mistaken
for a tap that selects a node. pointercancel is handled alongside pointerup,
since the browser can take a gesture away mid-flight.

Verified with synthetic two-finger gestures in Chromium: pinching out reduces the
camera radius, pinching in raises it, and a two-finger drag moves the camera
target while leaving the radius alone.

